    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n4090" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">as-sŏno</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ads-</span></b> , Jahn; <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ass-</span></b> ,
		Merk.), āre, v. n., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to sound to</i>, <i>respond to</i> (rare): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">plangentibus assonat Echo,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. M.
					3, 507</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">reparabilis adsonat Echo,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Pers.
					1, 102</span></i>
			.— With acc. of similar signif.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ut canorae aviculae concentus suaves
					adsonarent,</span>”
				<i>struck up</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">App. M. 11, p. 260</span></i>
			.</div>
